  "control": "CONTROL, NOT A CANDIDATE.  Identical transaction to the D-600 promotion -- the same 32 --bond-pad stitches, the same three requested nets, --partial --repair-planes -- with the pour-bond guard entirely OFF instead of reduced to the 34 tubes whose ends bond redundancy could NOT retire.  It is what D-599 ran on the UNBONDED board and it returns D-599's exact shape: /I2C_SCL_INT closes one edge, GND opens one, --repair-planes names GND as its candidate and cannot re-bond it, board 74 -> 74, REFUSED.  So the bonds alone are not what closes the edge, and neither is dropping the guard: with the REDUCED guard on, the router is pushed off the 34 tubes that are still load-bearing and finds a path that costs GND nothing, 74 -> 73.  The pre-filter, once its retired tubes are removed, is strictly BETTER than no pre-filter.",
